    'Veterinary installations demand clean cable execution, moisture-sealed cameras in treatment zones, and secure pharmacy vault coverage. Our Fort Worth technicians deliver professional systems tailored to animal hospitals.',
    'We serve general veterinary practices, twenty-four hour emergency and specialty animal hospitals, boarding facilities, and mixed and large-animal practices across Camp Bowie, Hulen, the near south side, the I-35W and AllianceTexas corridor, the Chisholm Trail Parkway growth band, and the surrounding communities of Keller, Southlake, Colleyville, Grapevine, Mansfield, Burleson, Saginaw, White Settlement, Arlington, and Weatherford. Older converted storefronts often need surface conduit in back of house, which we plan and price during the walk, while newer purpose-built hospitals can have pathway designed into the structured cabling before finish-out closes. Practices with barns, paddocks, or detached kennel buildings get exterior color night vision and wireless bridge links between structures. Wet zones receive IP67 metal housings rated for daily disinfectant washdown, and the recorder stays in a locked conditioned office. Our crews are local, licensed, and insured, with same-day service and footage export.',
